# The build context is uploaded to the daemon in full before anything is
# built, so anything here that the image does not need is pure wall-clock.
#
# `target` is the one that mattered: this file used to name `backend/target`,
# a path from an older layout that has not existed for a long time, so the
# real one was sent every time — 47 GB of build cache, on every `make scale`,
# before a single line was compiled.
.git
target
deploy
*.log

# Local benchmark history: read by a human, never by the build.
bench
